3.3.0 (not yet released)

#229: (pcollections) Add deserializers for PCollection `TreePSet`, `TreePMap`,
  `OrderedPMap` and `AmortizedPQueue` types
 (contributed by Vanya M)
#232: (guava) Invalid stringified `Range` and incomparable sorted elements throw
  raw runtime exceptions
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#233: (guava) `Nulls.SKIP` on immutable collection contents drops `null`s
  returned by value deserializer (also: report such `null`s, instead of
  throwing `NullPointerException`, for single-value, sorted, `Multiset` and
  `ImmutableMap` content)
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#245: (guava) `ImmutableSortedSet` / `ImmutableSortedMultiset` cannot be deserialized
  as `Object` with default typing
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#240: (eclipse-collections) Most types fail to round-trip with default typing enabled;
  primitive maps silently lose data
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#251: (eclipse-collections) `Pair` / `Triple` deserialization fails for raw types
  and implementation classes (default typing); `Triplet` read as `TripleImpl`
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#253: (guava) Avoid redundant copy when deserializing `Multimap` already
  of requested type (`ArrayListMultimap`, `HashMultimap`, `LinkedHashMultimap`)
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#256: (guava) Avoid boxing every element when deserializing `Ints.asList` (etc)
  primitive lists
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#258: (hppc) `BitSet` serialized up to allocated capacity (`size()`), not
  highest set bit: output array length changes accordingly
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#260: (hppc) Specialized `IntIndexedContainer` serializer never used (checks
  `JavaType.getClass()` instead of raw class)
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#262: (hppc) Avoid copying `ByteArrayList` / `CharArrayList` contents on
  serialization
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#264: (eclipse-collections) Avoid allocating a `char[]` per entry when serializing
  `char`-valued primitive maps
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#270: (eclipse-collections) Parse numeric primitive map keys the same way as
  `jackson-databind` does (using `NumberInput` etc)
 (fixed by @pjfanning)
#273: (guava) Report `null`s rejected by `Multimap`s and `Table`s as input mismatch;
  apply content null handling to single-value `Multimap`s (also: JSON `null` values
  for `ImmutableMap`s now reported, not silently dropped; use `Nulls.SKIP` to drop)
 (fixed by @cowtowncoder)
#274: (guava) Report current token (not start token) to `DeserializationProblemHandler`
  when value deserializer returns `null` for a structured (Object/Array) value
  (note: handlers now see `END_OBJECT` / `END_ARRAY`, not `START_OBJECT` / `START_ARRAY`;
  for `RangeSet`, actual token instead of `VALUE_NULL`)
 (fixed by @cowtowncoder)

